uch%20skill%20forecasts%20are%20based%20on%20the%20spread%20of%20ensemble%20forecasts%20(i.e.%20a%20set%20of%20alternative%20scenarios%20for%20the%20coming%20period)%20for%20a%20single%20prediction%20horizon%20or%20over%20a%20look-ahead%20period.%20It%20is%20shown%20on%20the%20test%20case%20of%20a%20Danish%20offshore%20wind%20farm%20how%20these%20prediction%20risk%20indices%20may%20be%20related%20to%20several%20levels%20of%20forecast%20uncertainty%20(and%20potential%20energy%20imbalances).%20Wind%20power%20ensemble%20predictions%20are%20derived%20from%20the%20conversion%20of%20ECMWF%20and%20NCEP%20ensemble%20forecasts%20of%20meteorological%20variables%20to%20wind%20power%20ensemble%20forecasts%2C%20as%20well%20as%20by%20a%20lagged%20average%20approach%20alternative.%20The%20ability%20of%20prediction%20risk%20indices%20calculated%20from%20the%20various%20types%20of%20ensembles%20forecasts%20to%20resolve%20among%20situations%20with%20different%20levels%20of%20uncertainty%20is%20discussed.%22%2C%22container-title%22%3A%22Applied%20Energy%22%2C%22issue%22%3A%227%22%2C%22note%22%3A%22Citation%20Key%3A%20Pinson09skillEnsWndPow%5Cnpublisher%3A%20Elsevier%5Cntex.owner%3A%20sotterson%5Cntex.timestamp%3A%202014.07.09%22%2C%22page%22%3A%221326%E2%80%931334%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22Skill%20forecasting%20from%20ensemble%20predictions%20of%20wind%20power%22%2C%22URL%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.sciencedirect.com%2Fscience%2Farticle%2Fpii%2FS0306261908002602%22%2C%22volume%22%3A%2286%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Pinson%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Pierre%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Nielsen%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22H%20Aa%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Madsen%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Henrik%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Kariniotakis%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Georges%22%7D%5D%2C%22issued%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222009%22%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citation-key%22%3A%22Pinson09skillEnsWndPow%22%7D%7D%5D\" data-schema-version=\"9\"><p>Jonczy25EpidemiologyClinicalManifestation</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>